   "variant": "generic",
   "children": [
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "level": "p",
     "text": "Austin answers",
     "classes": []
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "level": "h2",
     "text": "Where Can I Get an AI Logo Fixed in Austin?",
     "align": "left",
     "classes": []
    },
    {
     "t": "text",
     "html": "<p>Logo Design Austin handles AI logo cleanup for businesses across the city and Central Texas, entirely remotely. There is no office visit and no traffic on MoPac; you upload the file, talk with a designer by phone or text, and approve proofs from your phone.</p><h3>AI logo cleanup in 78701, 78702, 78704 and across Austin</h3><p>A coffee trailer in East Austin (78702), a boutique on South Congress (78704), a startup near the Domain (78758) or a law office downtown (78701) all run into the same wall: an AI image that looks fine on Instagram and falls apart at the print shop. We rebuild it as vector artwork and send files your printer, sign shop or uniform supplier can use the first time.</p><h3>Will an Austin sign or print shop accept my AI logo as it is?</h3><p>In most cases, no. Sign makers, vinyl cutters and embroidery shops around Austin ask for EPS, AI, SVG or a vector PDF. A PNG from an image generator prints soft when enlarged and cannot be cut or stitched cleanly. After cleanup you can hand any vendor the correct file without a second round of back-and-forth.</p><h3>Should I fix my AI logo or start over with a new design?</h3><p>If the concept suits your business, fixing it is usually quicker and costs less than a brand-new logo. If the idea has deeper issues, such as being hard to read at small sizes or looking too close to an existing brand, we will say so plainly and point you to <a href=\"/custom-design/\">custom logo design</a> instead. For reference, a new custom logo at Logo Design Austin is priced from $125 to $175.</p>",
     "align": "left",
     "classes": []
    },
    {
     "t": "container",
     "classes": [],
     "dir": "row",
     "wrap": true,
     "width": 100,
     "boxed": false,
